(1726015, 234505, 39349, '<td valign="top">Pretty nice photo but; where''s the bubble?</td>', 'Pretty nice photo but; where''s the bubble?', '2005-09-21 01:45:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726055, 232306, 3554, '<td valign="top">I like the colors a lot, but they look more like water droplets than bubbles to me.</td>', 'I like the colors a lot, but they look more like water droplets than bubbles to me.', '2005-09-21 02:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726057, 231925, 3554, '<td valign="top">Love the colors. It seems more of a focus on water splashing than on bubbles per se but it''s still a cool shot.</td>', 'Love the colors. It seems more of a focus on water splashing than on bubbles per se but it''s still a cool shot.', '2005-09-21 03:00:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726058, 231786, 36377, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to seen the edges cropped off to make it a vertical composition.</td>', 'I would have liked to seen the edges cropped off to make it a vertical composition.', '2005-09-21 03:02:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726061, 233410, 3554, '<td valign="top">Maybe I''m not getting it, but I''m not sure how this fits in with Bubbles, looks like a water droplet to me. Cool picture though.</td>', 'Maybe I''m not getting it, but I''m not sure how this fits in with Bubbles, looks like a water droplet to me. Cool picture though.', '2005-09-21 03:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726067, 234624, 16241, '<td valign="top">cute</td>', 'cute', '2005-09-21 03:09:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726069, 234367, 4281, '<td valign="top">Now, I can understand that the model doesn''t want to be nude in the photo but wearing a bikini in the bath is a bit, what shall we call it, strange, don''t ya think?<br/>As it is her position in the bath is very very bizarre and I think it would have looked much better to have her body submerged in the water. <br/>Another thing, what is she looking at?? Why isn''t she instead looking at the camera or frankly just anything else than what is to her left. <br/>It''s also quite irritating to not have the entire right hand in the frame and you leave a bit too much space above her head.<br/> <br/>Now, if the point here was to create a strange looking picture, with the bubble-gum and the woman''s uncomfortable position,  I''d say you''ve failed in your quest. As it is the picture isn''t strange enough to serve that purpose. Perhaps with a bit more exotic lightning or framing or Photoshop-work or  just a bit more creative hairdo it would have worked to that purpose but not as it. <br/> <br/>Sorry if I''m a bit harsh but I feel the original idea, a bubble-gum in a bubble-bath was quite neat but you''ve flunked on implementation. Better luck next time, I guess. :)</td>', 'Now, I can understand that the model doesn''t want to be nude in the photo but wearing a bikini in the bath is a bit, what shall we call it, strange, don''t ya think?As it is her position in the bath is very very bizarre and I think it would have looked much better to have her body submerged in the water. Another thing, what is she looking at?? Why isn''t she instead looking at the camera or frankly just anything else than what is to her left. It''s also quite irritating to not have the entire right hand in the frame and you leave a bit too much space above her head. Now, if the point here was to create a strange looking picture, with the bubble-gum and the woman''s uncomfortable position,  I''d say you''ve failed in your quest. As it is the picture isn''t strange enough to serve that purpose. Perhaps with a bit more exotic lightning or framing or Photoshop-work or  just a bit more creative hairdo it would have worked to that purpose but not as it.  Sorry if I''m a bit harsh but I feel the original idea, a bubble-gum in a bubble-bath was quite neat but you''ve flunked on implementation. Better luck next time, I guess. :)', '2005-09-21 03:13:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726082, 233403, 15212, '<td valign="top">It''s a beautiful picture but in my opinion, water droplets are not bubbles.</td>', 'It''s a beautiful picture but in my opinion, water droplets are not bubbles.', '2005-09-21 03:21:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726085, 231899, 36377, '<td valign="top">The left side looks a little odd. I might have cropped it out. Still a wonderful shot though.</td>', 'The left side looks a little odd. I might have cropped it out. Still a wonderful shot though.', '2005-09-21 03:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726089, 233831, 15212, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how you did it but it''s very effective! The only nitpick I have is the ''bruised'' looking hand. I''m guessing it''s from the lighting you used?</td>', 'I don''t know how you did it but it''s very effective! The only nitpick I have is the ''bruised'' looking hand. I''m guessing it''s from the lighting you used?', '2005-09-21 03:26:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726090, 234498, 43463, '<td valign="top">The composition is good on this photo. The viewer''s main attention is tightly focused  on the subject and the objects surrounding her. However it does suffer from lack of sharp focus on the bubbles and on the subjects face. While the girl is mostly in focus the bubbles in the forefront are not. The bubbles have a very fuzzy and soft look to them and while that may add to the dreamy aspect to it, I still think it could have been better if it was more sharply in focus. And admittingly bubbles are not an easy subject to capture. Not knowing what camera you are working with I am limited  to dispensing broad advice : if you have a camera where you can set the aperature I would recommend the highest you can set it (the higher the number the less ''light'' is let in through the ''lens''). Why close down the aperature to let less light in? The reason is that it gives a greater depth of field to the shot not to mention greatly enhances the sharpness of the foreground and background of the shot. So that even thought the focus may be centered on the model the bubbles in the foreground would be in sharp focus too. Hope this helps.</td>', 'The composition is good on this photo. The viewer''s main attention is tightly focused  on the subject and the objects surrounding her. However it does suffer from lack of sharp focus on the bubbles and on the subjects face. While the girl is mostly in focus the bubbles in the forefront are not. The bubbles have a very fuzzy and soft look to them and while that may add to the dreamy aspect to it, I still think it could have been better if it was more sharply in focus. And admittingly bubbles are not an easy subject to capture. Not knowing what camera you are working with I am limited  to dispensing broad advice : if you have a camera where you can set the aperature I would recommend the highest you can set it (the higher the number the less ''light'' is let in through the ''lens''). Why close down the aperature to let less light in? The reason is that it gives a greater depth of field to the shot not to mention greatly enhances the sharpness of the foreground and background of the shot. So that even thought the focus may be centered on the model the bubbles in the foreground would be in sharp focus too. Hope this helps.', '2005-09-21 03:27:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726095, 233402, 16241, '<td valign="top">awesome!  thanks for a NEW fav.</td>', 'awesome!  thanks for a NEW fav.', '2005-09-21 03:28:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726099, 234360, 15212, '<td valign="top">If this were a water drop challenge I would give this a very high score, but it''s a bubble challenge. Sorry.</td>', 'If this were a water drop challenge I would give this a very high score, but it''s a bubble challenge. Sorry.', '2005-09-21 03:30:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726104, 232517, 43463, '<td valign="top">A sweet and endearing capture. The child''s face has a nice little smile as he looks at the bubbles on his hand. He does seem to be pondering the question that all children seem to ask" Where do bubbles go?" It is that smile and a bathtub full of bubbles that help invoke the ideas of a playful childhood. This photo can  invoke in the viewer, fond memories of their own childhood. The lighting is very good in this shot with all elements appearing to be cast in a natural light that compliments the overall photo.</td>', 'A sweet and endearing capture. The child''s face has a nice little smile as he looks at the bubbles on his hand. He does seem to be pondering the question that all children seem to ask" Where do bubbles go?" It is that smile and a bathtub full of bubbles that help invoke the ideas of a playful childhood. This photo can  invoke in the viewer, fond memories of their own childhood. The lighting is very good in this shot with all elements appearing to be cast in a natural light that compliments the overall photo.', '2005-09-21 03:32:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726112, 233789, 43463, '<td valign="top">Now the composition in this shot is fabulous! The ruby red shoes with just a peak of a blue and white checked dress invokes the imagery of Dorothy from the Wizard of Oz. The bubble in the forefront of the shot makes the viewer think of Glenda the Good Witch (whom in the movie at least) appears from a bubble. The only thing that this suffers from is the fact that while the shoes,feet, and dress are in perfect focus the soap bubble is not. It would strengthen the composition if that soap bubble in the immediate forground was also in tight focus. Not knowing what camera you have I am going to give a broad suggestion: If you can manually set the aperature on the camera you might want to set it at it''s highest number such that is closes down how much light is let in through the "open shutter". The reason for this is that it will give you a greater depth of field and objects in the forground and background will be in sharper focus. It also might be a good idea to have a tripod or a make shift tripod so the even the slightest movement from the photographer does not affect the focus on the shot. Even then, I found that bubbles are very challenging to work with. Oh and cudos to you for your patience and persistance for this shot. It must not have been easy to get the bubble you wanted to float into the scene.</td>', 'Now the composition in this shot is fabulous! The ruby red shoes with just a peak of a blue and white checked dress invokes the imagery of Dorothy from the Wizard of Oz. The bubble in the forefront of the shot makes the viewer think of Glenda the Good Witch (whom in the movie at least) appears from a bubble. The only thing that this suffers from is the fact that while the shoes,feet, and dress are in perfect focus the soap bubble is not. It would strengthen the composition if that soap bubble in the immediate forground was also in tight focus. Not knowing what camera you have I am going to give a broad suggestion: If you can manually set the aperature on the camera you might want to set it at it''s highest number such that is closes down how much light is let in through the "open shutter". The reason for this is that it will give you a greater depth of field and objects in the forground and background will be in sharper focus. It also might be a good idea to have a tripod or a make shift tripod so the even the slightest movement from the photographer does not affect the focus on the shot. Even then, I found that bubbles are very challenging to work with. Oh and cudos to you for your patience and persistance for this shot. It must not have been easy to get the bubble you wanted to float into the scene.', '2005-09-21 03:43:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726116, 231949, 15212, '<td valign="top">Accually, those are natures water drops, not what I consider bubbles. Still, it''s a nice photo.</td>', 'Accually, those are natures water drops, not what I consider bubbles. Still, it''s a nice photo.', '2005-09-21 03:47:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726124, 233402, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is an adorable and sweet capture! The expression on the child''s face is so exuberant and so full of fun and laughter that one cannot help but to smile as they view this photo. The black background is the perfect backdrop for this image for the viewer really gets to see the bubbles without them being ''lost'' in a background with too many distracting object. Not to mention the the choice of a black background makes the bubbles pop out more than a white one would.  The only critique I have on this shot is that I think if you had included more space in the upper half of the photo to accomendate a possible bubble that is just out of reach of this child. He/she seems to be reaching for a bubble that is not shown in the frame. If that bubble was included in the frame it would have established a even stronger connection of bubble play between the child and the bubbles floating around him/her.</td>', 'This is an adorable and sweet capture! The expression on the child''s face is so exuberant and so full of fun and laughter that one cannot help but to smile as they view this photo. The black background is the perfect backdrop for this image for the viewer really gets to see the bubbles without them being ''lost'' in a background with too many distracting object. Not to mention the the choice of a black background makes the bubbles pop out more than a white one would.  The only critique I have on this shot is that I think if you had included more space in the upper half of the photo to accomendate a possible bubble that is just out of reach of this child. He/she seems to be reaching for a bubble that is not shown in the frame. If that bubble was included in the frame it would have established a even stronger connection of bubble play between the child and the bubbles floating around him/her.', '2005-09-21 03:57:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726126, 234357, 43463, '<td valign="top">I like the composition on this photo. The deep rich brown hues against the white coffee cup really help to invoke not only the visual of coffee but it also invokes the taste and smell of fresh brewed coffee in the morning. My only critique is that while the focus is tightly centered on the bubbles within the cup it is too zoomed in. The overall image would be strengthen if you had cropped the image to include just the a bit more of the curve of the coffee cup in the top left hand corner. The curve of the coffee cup would mimic and complement the curves seen in the bubbles not to mention give the eye another pleasing curve to follow as they explore the contents of this photo.</td>', 'I like the composition on this photo. The deep rich brown hues against the white coffee cup really help to invoke not only the visual of coffee but it also invokes the taste and smell of fresh brewed coffee in the morning. My only critique is that while the focus is tightly centered on the bubbles within the cup it is too zoomed in. The overall image would be strengthen if you had cropped the image to include just the a bit more of the curve of the coffee cup in the top left hand corner. The curve of the coffee cup would mimic and complement the curves seen in the bubbles not to mention give the eye another pleasing curve to follow as they explore the contents of this photo.', '2005-09-21 04:05:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726132, 234062, 42404, '<td valign="top">It''s a little pixelated, but wherever the red color is coming from is nice.</td>', 'It''s a little pixelated, but wherever the red color is coming from is nice.', '2005-09-21 04:26:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1726134, 234467, 29474, '<td valign="top">Because of the size of this picture, it is a little difficult to see the bubbles. It also seems to be out-of-focus. The blue is a great colour.</td>', 'Because of the size of this picture, it is a little difficult to see the bubbles. It also seems to be out-of-focus. The blue is a great colour.', '2005-09-21 04:46:44.000000', NULL, 1),
