(1733240, 233785, 40580, '<td valign="top">I''m curious about your point of focus.  It''s on the rim of the cup?  I would''ve placed it on the bubbles or the spoon.</td>', 'I''m curious about your point of focus.  It''s on the rim of the cup?  I would''ve placed it on the bubbles or the spoon.', '2005-09-23 11:01:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733299, 233831, 43463, '<td valign="top">The circumstances are that this poor model must have had to pose for a quite a long time to get this shot to appear like it is here. Not an easy feat since I can see that she is crouching there in a corner. Her hands are perfectly positioned to make it appear as if she is pressing on the bubble. And she seems to be looking right at the straw that created this bubble. I would love to learn how you accomplished this shot - at first glance I thought it can''t be a straight photo but I see that this has been validated. Whew, this must have taken alot of positioning, planning, and timing....Technically everything is perfect. My only two  nits about the shot is the colors - the purplish-blues are fine and add to the mood of "being blue or caught in a prision" but there is little too much of an orange cast on the person''s hand and arm that is holding the bubble that clashes with those purple and blue hues. A warm hue can mix with a cool hue effectively but in this shot it just pop out to much that they are competing with one another instead of complementing. The other critique is that I would have shown the full hand and less of the arm - as that it is the hand that holds this woman''s "prision" it should be more in the shot. <br/> <br/>Nonetheless, great job.</td>', 'The circumstances are that this poor model must have had to pose for a quite a long time to get this shot to appear like it is here. Not an easy feat since I can see that she is crouching there in a corner. Her hands are perfectly positioned to make it appear as if she is pressing on the bubble. And she seems to be looking right at the straw that created this bubble. I would love to learn how you accomplished this shot - at first glance I thought it can''t be a straight photo but I see that this has been validated. Whew, this must have taken alot of positioning, planning, and timing....Technically everything is perfect. My only two  nits about the shot is the colors - the purplish-blues are fine and add to the mood of "being blue or caught in a prision" but there is little too much of an orange cast on the person''s hand and arm that is holding the bubble that clashes with those purple and blue hues. A warm hue can mix with a cool hue effectively but in this shot it just pop out to much that they are competing with one another instead of complementing. The other critique is that I would have shown the full hand and less of the arm - as that it is the hand that holds this woman''s "prision" it should be more in the shot.  Nonetheless, great job.', '2005-09-23 11:24:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733310, 234523, 43463, '<td valign="top">This photo has good potential. I like that it plays on the "Sleeping Beauty" fable. The positives of this shot: I like how the soft pink and slight blue hues seen on the bubble compliment those same colors on the models eyelid. They appear to have the same shades and this further establishes a connection between the two objects. This photo plays with the story Sleeping Beauty but it is Sleeping Bubbles.<br/> <br/>The negatives: The dark background behind the models head in not complementary to the photo - To further establish the connection to the tale of Sleeping beauty you could have done several things : shown us her hair gently curled on a pillow or just a colorful pillow that would have brighted up the space AND complimented the color schemes already present in the photo. There is a little too much overexposure or show of the flash on the lower right hand side of the bubble: it washes out those beautiful soft pastel hues of pink and blue not to mention distracts the eye. And lastly, it would have been lovely to have seen those lovely eyelashes more sharply focused so that it makes an even stronger connection to the words  sleep and beauty.</td>', 'This photo has good potential. I like that it plays on the "Sleeping Beauty" fable. The positives of this shot: I like how the soft pink and slight blue hues seen on the bubble compliment those same colors on the models eyelid. They appear to have the same shades and this further establishes a connection between the two objects. This photo plays with the story Sleeping Beauty but it is Sleeping Bubbles. The negatives: The dark background behind the models head in not complementary to the photo - To further establish the connection to the tale of Sleeping beauty you could have done several things : shown us her hair gently curled on a pillow or just a colorful pillow that would have brighted up the space AND complimented the color schemes already present in the photo. There is a little too much overexposure or show of the flash on the lower right hand side of the bubble: it washes out those beautiful soft pastel hues of pink and blue not to mention distracts the eye. And lastly, it would have been lovely to have seen those lovely eyelashes more sharply focused so that it makes an even stronger connection to the words  sleep and beauty.', '2005-09-23 11:34:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733318, 234185, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is a nice candid photo of a child taking a bubble bath. Technically: Things are in nice sharp focus but the composition could have been more tightly framed around just  the child''s head his bubble crown.  The other  critique is that you title this Bubble Fun but this poor child looks as if he is having anything but.... His lips are tightly pursed and he seems unhappy. A smile upon his face woud have made this shot more appealing and play into the title better.  Instead of fun that we stereotypically associate with a bubble bath I am left wondering what he is so unhappy about.</td>', 'This is a nice candid photo of a child taking a bubble bath. Technically: Things are in nice sharp focus but the composition could have been more tightly framed around just  the child''s head his bubble crown.  The other  critique is that you title this Bubble Fun but this poor child looks as if he is having anything but.... His lips are tightly pursed and he seems unhappy. A smile upon his face woud have made this shot more appealing and play into the title better.  Instead of fun that we stereotypically associate with a bubble bath I am left wondering what he is so unhappy about.', '2005-09-23 11:41:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733322, 234275, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is a nice candid shot. And how fortunate that the girl is wearing a shirt that sports the word "pop"!  It adds a little ironic variety to the photo considering she is surrounded by delicate bubbles that could "pop" at any moment. The thing that would have improved this candid photo would have been if you could have captured a smile on her face as well.</td>', 'This is a nice candid shot. And how fortunate that the girl is wearing a shirt that sports the word "pop"!  It adds a little ironic variety to the photo considering she is surrounded by delicate bubbles that could "pop" at any moment. The thing that would have improved this candid photo would have been if you could have captured a smile on her face as well.', '2005-09-23 11:45:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733330, 233050, 37776, '<td valign="top">Wow!good idea!:)</td>', 'Wow!good idea!:)', '2005-09-23 11:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733338, 231905, 43463, '<td valign="top">An interesting composition that presents the idea to the viewer that the earth can be just as fragile as a soap bubble. Two things that could greatly improve this shot and move it from o.k. to really good: One) To strengthen the imagery that the earth is fragile and "balanced" precariously it would have been better to orient the bubble holder under the bubble/earth. That way gravity (a play on both meaning here) of the sitiuation is present: The earth is more in a position to just fall (instead of slip off and fall) just like the bubble can pop at any moment. Second, the bubble needed to be more sharply in focus and more visible...here in this take it is too faint in areas and because of that we notice the "earth" much more readily than that of the soap bubble.</td>', 'An interesting composition that presents the idea to the viewer that the earth can be just as fragile as a soap bubble. Two things that could greatly improve this shot and move it from o.k. to really good: One) To strengthen the imagery that the earth is fragile and "balanced" precariously it would have been better to orient the bubble holder under the bubble/earth. That way gravity (a play on both meaning here) of the sitiuation is present: The earth is more in a position to just fall (instead of slip off and fall) just like the bubble can pop at any moment. Second, the bubble needed to be more sharply in focus and more visible...here in this take it is too faint in areas and because of that we notice the "earth" much more readily than that of the soap bubble.', '2005-09-23 11:53:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733342, 232933, 37893, '<td valign="top">Jutilda? Is this you? This is such an awesome capture :) How did you manage to get this shot? Great colors. The expression on his face is spot on. 10</td>', 'Jutilda? Is this you? This is such an awesome capture :) How did you manage to get this shot? Great colors. The expression on his face is spot on. 10', '2005-09-23 11:56:43.000000', NULL, 1),
