(1733584, 231849, 39664, '<td valign="top">I question what kind of "bubble" that is?  Technically this shot is awesome but how is the bubble created and does it contain air or is it water?  It looks like a piece of glass that magnifies for reading or doing crafts.</td>', 'I question what kind of "bubble" that is?  Technically this shot is awesome but how is the bubble created and does it contain air or is it water?  It looks like a piece of glass that magnifies for reading or doing crafts.', '2005-09-23 13:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1733585, 234566, 27482, '<td valign="top">I was just going to let this slide but I figured you might want to hear what I thought about this picture even though it might sting a little bit.  Just keep in mind that this is just my opinion and what the hell do I know anyways...<br/> <br/>At first I didn´t even seen any bubbles.  There is simply way way way too much going on in this shot in the backround that my eye immediately went for the cars in the backround, then the street signs, then the licence plate of the Huyundai and finally the guys and after about 5 seconds looking and looking I finally noticed a couple of bubbles drifting along there on the right side.  In short, WAY too much going on in the shot and that makes the bubbles seem like an insignificant portion of the shot, I wouldn´t be surprised if many people have voted on this shot as being off topic, however, I won´t be one of them.<br/> <br/>I think making this shot sepia was a bad choice as it makes the guys and bubbles really blend into the backround and also I would say that having the whole scene in the DOF is also a bad choice but I don´t know if you simply had to do it that way, depends on what camera you used obviously.  I still like the lighting, it´s well exposed and in focus and nothing wrong with that department.<br/> <br/>Anyway, ended up giving this 4...  Sorry for the rant and if you disagree then just completely ignore me, like I said, what the hell do I know :o)</td>', 'I was just going to let this slide but I figured you might want to hear what I thought about this picture even though it might sting a little bit.  Just keep in mind that this is just my opinion and what the hell do I know anyways... At first I didn´t even seen any bubbles.  There is simply way way way too much going on in this shot in the backround that my eye immediately went for the cars in the backround, then the street signs, then the licence plate of the Huyundai and finally the guys and after about 5 seconds looking and looking I finally noticed a couple of bubbles drifting along there on the right side.  In short, WAY too much going on in the shot and that makes the bubbles seem like an insignificant portion of the shot, I wouldn´t be surprised if many people have voted on this shot as being off topic, however, I won´t be one of them. I think making this shot sepia was a bad choice as it makes the guys and bubbles really blend into the backround and also I would say that having the whole scene in the DOF is also a bad choice but I don´t know if you simply had to do it that way, depends on what camera you used obviously.  I still like the lighting, it´s well exposed and in focus and nothing wrong with that department. Anyway, ended up giving this 4...  Sorry for the rant and if you disagree then just completely ignore me, like I said, what the hell do I know :o)', '2005-09-23 13:53:59.000000', NULL, 1),
