(1737991, 233391, 41675, '<td valign="top">These strands remind me more of fiber optics than bubbles. I like the colors against the black background.</td>', 'These strands remind me more of fiber optics than bubbles. I like the colors against the black background.', '2005-09-25 21:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1737993, 234481, 41675, '<td valign="top">Bumping up after second look. I like this in black and white. To me, this also would have worked in the Greeting Card challenge.</td>', 'Bumping up after second look. I like this in black and white. To me, this also would have worked in the Greeting Card challenge.', '2005-09-25 21:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1737996, 233037, 41675, '<td valign="top">For me, this seems like a bit of a stretch for the bubble entry, but I think having this in black and white works.</td>', 'For me, this seems like a bit of a stretch for the bubble entry, but I think having this in black and white works.', '2005-09-25 21:33:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1737999, 233003, 41675, '<td valign="top">Good concept. I like the angle and opposing, graphic like treatment of colors. A bit more focus and crispness and I would have scored it higher.</td>', 'Good concept. I like the angle and opposing, graphic like treatment of colors. A bit more focus and crispness and I would have scored it higher.', '2005-09-25 21:34:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738007, 233048, 41675, '<td valign="top">My favorite area is the one bubble itself. Bumping up after second look.</td>', 'My favorite area is the one bubble itself. Bumping up after second look.', '2005-09-25 21:38:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738010, 232257, 41675, '<td valign="top">This is a very beautiful landscape. For me...it''s stretching it to fit the challenge, but still a very beautiful shot.</td>', 'This is a very beautiful landscape. For me...it''s stretching it to fit the challenge, but still a very beautiful shot.', '2005-09-25 21:39:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738023, 233892, 41675, '<td valign="top">I like the different take on the challenge. Bumping up after second look.</td>', 'I like the different take on the challenge. Bumping up after second look.', '2005-09-25 21:50:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738026, 231763, 41675, '<td valign="top">For me, I find photos more appealing when the main subject is slightly off-centered or taken from a different angle. Maybe a bit tighter focus on the glass. I like your idea though - keep going :-)</td>', 'For me, I find photos more appealing when the main subject is slightly off-centered or taken from a different angle. Maybe a bit tighter focus on the glass. I like your idea though - keep going :-)', '2005-09-25 21:52:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738043, 233783, 41675, '<td valign="top">Nice closeup. I like the uniformity of all the tiny bubbles. Bumping up after a second look.</td>', 'Nice closeup. I like the uniformity of all the tiny bubbles. Bumping up after a second look.', '2005-09-25 22:03:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738052, 233746, 11923, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous color, good focus.  I love the graininess of the image, gives it some very nice texture.  Is this one of those sand/water things that you turn upside down and the sand slowly sifts its way down to make neat landscape shapes?  Lighting is great and of course bubbles are present.  Nicely done, I gave a 7.</td>', 'Gorgeous color, good focus.  I love the graininess of the image, gives it some very nice texture.  Is this one of those sand/water things that you turn upside down and the sand slowly sifts its way down to make neat landscape shapes?  Lighting is great and of course bubbles are present.  Nicely done, I gave a 7.', '2005-09-25 22:09:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738057, 232174, 41675, '<td valign="top">I wonder how this would look if you were to crop out the dark, blurry area at the bottom and rotate the photo clockwise a bit? Good advertisement for the beer, though compared to other entries it doesn''t really speak "bubbles" to me.</td>', 'I wonder how this would look if you were to crop out the dark, blurry area at the bottom and rotate the photo clockwise a bit? Good advertisement for the beer, though compared to other entries it doesn''t really speak "bubbles" to me.', '2005-09-25 22:11:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738058, 232482, 41675, '<td valign="top">Looks a little grainy on my screen, but it could be the look were going for.  A bit more focus on the bubbles and grass blades and maybe bump up the saturation, this would really "pop" (sorry, couldn''t resist) :-)</td>', 'Looks a little grainy on my screen, but it could be the look were going for.  A bit more focus on the bubbles and grass blades and maybe bump up the saturation, this would really "pop" (sorry, couldn''t resist) :-)', '2005-09-25 22:13:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738060, 234298, 41675, '<td valign="top">I''m not usually a fan of filter effects through a photo-editing program, but in this case, your chosen effects work ok. I wish there was a bit more color, but a nice tone on tone photo.</td>', 'I''m not usually a fan of filter effects through a photo-editing program, but in this case, your chosen effects work ok. I wish there was a bit more color, but a nice tone on tone photo.', '2005-09-25 22:14:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738066, 232605, 11923, '<td valign="top">Hm.. this certainly meets the challenge but I''m afraid that is all it has going for it at the moment.  Clearly the bubble is meant to be the focus of the image and I think this could be a great idea if a few things were changed:<br/> <br/>Background:  Rumpled and grey and doesn''t do much for the image.  I would recommend a black for this type of photograph.<br/> <br/>Focus:  is GREAT.. unfortunately.. its on the wrong thing - the background.  The focus should be centered on the bubble and thus let the background fuzz away, this I can see is difficult due to the nature of bubbles, cameras tend to have a problem finding them to center on.<br/> <br/>Lighting:  The lighting is actually pretty good, if there was a way to center it more spotlight-esque only on the bubble, that *might* give the camera more help in focusing there too.  I can''t be sure though.  Still your use of light was good.<br/> <br/>Composition:  Here''s a biggie.  Right now you simply have a bubble with nothing too exciting going on.  This CAN work, but the other elements of the image (background, focus, etc) are working against you and so the simplistic approach didn''t really fly.  I do like the idea behind the image immensely, I can envision a simple, classicly beautiful perfectly rounded glowing bubble suspended against a black background of some sort.. simple and lovely.  So the idea and intent is there, it just didn''t manifest itself this time around and led to a fairly dull image.<br/> <br/>You have a good eye and vision, just need to work on the technique a bit to bring those up to match.  I gave a 3.</td>', 'Hm.. this certainly meets the challenge but I''m afraid that is all it has going for it at the moment.  Clearly the bubble is meant to be the focus of the image and I think this could be a great idea if a few things were changed: Background:  Rumpled and grey and doesn''t do much for the image.  I would recommend a black for this type of photograph. Focus:  is GREAT.. unfortunately.. its on the wrong thing - the background.  The focus should be centered on the bubble and thus let the background fuzz away, this I can see is difficult due to the nature of bubbles, cameras tend to have a problem finding them to center on. Lighting:  The lighting is actually pretty good, if there was a way to center it more spotlight-esque only on the bubble, that *might* give the camera more help in focusing there too.  I can''t be sure though.  Still your use of light was good. Composition:  Here''s a biggie.  Right now you simply have a bubble with nothing too exciting going on.  This CAN work, but the other elements of the image (background, focus, etc) are working against you and so the simplistic approach didn''t really fly.  I do like the idea behind the image immensely, I can envision a simple, classicly beautiful perfectly rounded glowing bubble suspended against a black background of some sort.. simple and lovely.  So the idea and intent is there, it just didn''t manifest itself this time around and led to a fairly dull image. You have a good eye and vision, just need to work on the technique a bit to bring those up to match.  I gave a 3.', '2005-09-25 22:19:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738067, 233904, 41675, '<td valign="top">A very cool sculpture. The thing that makes me smile though is the bird sitting at the top. Is that a real bird?</td>', 'A very cool sculpture. The thing that makes me smile though is the bird sitting at the top. Is that a real bird?', '2005-09-25 22:20:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738068, 233772, 41675, '<td valign="top">The flash bounce off the glass is a bit bright. Sometimes changing your angle to glass will diminish or even eliminate that glare. Good concept though.</td>', 'The flash bounce off the glass is a bit bright. Sometimes changing your angle to glass will diminish or even eliminate that glare. Good concept though.', '2005-09-25 22:21:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738071, 231763, 11923, '<td valign="top">Certainly foamy and bubbly. The lighting is okay (some detail loss there) and the focus is decent.  The composition however really brings the potential of this image down.  The background used is uninspired and makes me as the viewer think "snapshot".  I would recommend a single colored cloth to help isolate the focus of the image - black would be good ONLY if you decided to use the lighting to its advantage and play off the amber colors of the beer.  If you''re mostly wanting to highlight the foam, I''d say a much tighter crop so only a part of the glass was showing and lighting.. maybe from a bottom up sort of direction?  Not sure how that''d look in practice.  Also the subject being so centered is a bit boring, maybe create some negative space and more interest by pushing it to the left or right, so only half the glass is showing.  Might be an idea.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'Certainly foamy and bubbly. The lighting is okay (some detail loss there) and the focus is decent.  The composition however really brings the potential of this image down.  The background used is uninspired and makes me as the viewer think "snapshot".  I would recommend a single colored cloth to help isolate the focus of the image - black would be good ONLY if you decided to use the lighting to its advantage and play off the amber colors of the beer.  If you''re mostly wanting to highlight the foam, I''d say a much tighter crop so only a part of the glass was showing and lighting.. maybe from a bottom up sort of direction?  Not sure how that''d look in practice.  Also the subject being so centered is a bit boring, maybe create some negative space and more interest by pushing it to the left or right, so only half the glass is showing.  Might be an idea.  I gave a 4.', '2005-09-25 22:22:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738082, 234607, 11923, '<td valign="top">Bubbly indeed.  Doesn''t draw me in as a viewer.  The lighting is faded and its making the image a bit dulled out - I can''t tell if the browner bubbles are because of dirt (as referenced by the title) or because of use of flash/lighting that''s browned them out.  Also its muting some of the details of the bubbles, focus is a bit soft too but that can work for you here.  Border.. not a fan, the light grey/purple only enhances the washed out nature.<br/> <br/>I think this could have had some real pop and impact if you used the body''s natural form to your advantage.  Highlight the curvature of the back and/or shoulders with a sheen of foamy bubbles and let the light trace that curve.   Heck, could even get humorous and make a bubble diaper.  Give the viewer something to take a second look at, right now its a bit flat and I have no inclination to lose myself in the image.  I gave a 3.</td>', 'Bubbly indeed.  Doesn''t draw me in as a viewer.  The lighting is faded and its making the image a bit dulled out - I can''t tell if the browner bubbles are because of dirt (as referenced by the title) or because of use of flash/lighting that''s browned them out.  Also its muting some of the details of the bubbles, focus is a bit soft too but that can work for you here.  Border.. not a fan, the light grey/purple only enhances the washed out nature. I think this could have had some real pop and impact if you used the body''s natural form to your advantage.  Highlight the curvature of the back and/or shoulders with a sheen of foamy bubbles and let the light trace that curve.   Heck, could even get humorous and make a bubble diaper.  Give the viewer something to take a second look at, right now its a bit flat and I have no inclination to lose myself in the image.  I gave a 3.', '2005-09-25 22:27:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738086, 232818, 11923, '<td valign="top">Ha, I used to do this as a kid, drove my mother bonkers.<br/> <br/>This has some real potential.  Nice strong line with the straw, which also provides a definite contrast.  The blue and white of course make for some nice crispness and the bubbles give it a lighthearted feel.  Unfortunately, these positives are nearly hidden by the blown out white and the soft focus.  Had all the lines (bubbles, straw, curve of cup) been nice and crisp I could see this really having a "wow" factor to it.  As it stands it seems a bit snapshotty to me.  Still it meets the challenge and has a good idea behind it and the composition in general is very nice.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'Ha, I used to do this as a kid, drove my mother bonkers. This has some real potential.  Nice strong line with the straw, which also provides a definite contrast.  The blue and white of course make for some nice crispness and the bubbles give it a lighthearted feel.  Unfortunately, these positives are nearly hidden by the blown out white and the soft focus.  Had all the lines (bubbles, straw, curve of cup) been nice and crisp I could see this really having a "wow" factor to it.  As it stands it seems a bit snapshotty to me.  Still it meets the challenge and has a good idea behind it and the composition in general is very nice.  I gave a 4.', '2005-09-25 22:30:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738093, 233831, 3306, '<td valign="top">Beautifully creative. Should be near the top. Great job.</td>', 'Beautifully creative. Should be near the top. Great job.', '2005-09-25 22:32:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738098, 233050, 3306, '<td valign="top">Wow, how many shots did it take to get this one right. Great job.</td>', 'Wow, how many shots did it take to get this one right. Great job.', '2005-09-25 22:33:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738100, 231904, 11923, '<td valign="top">Cute image.  I like the uniqueness of it.  Good color and the bubble is nicely deliniated.  I like the composition as far as using the curved flower coming from out of the top of the image, but I''m afraid the choice of bordering ruins it for me.  The white totally overwhelms the image and the sharp contrast draws me out of what should be the focal point of the photograph (the flower/bubble) and instead thrusts me into the play of the black and white against each other.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'Cute image.  I like the uniqueness of it.  Good color and the bubble is nicely deliniated.  I like the composition as far as using the curved flower coming from out of the top of the image, but I''m afraid the choice of bordering ruins it for me.  The white totally overwhelms the image and the sharp contrast draws me out of what should be the focal point of the photograph (the flower/bubble) and instead thrusts me into the play of the black and white against each other.  I gave a 4.', '2005-09-25 22:33:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738102, 231905, 3306, '<td valign="top">Nicely done and very creative.</td>', 'Nicely done and very creative.', '2005-09-25 22:33:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738106, 234406, 11923, '<td valign="top">Yikes.. what IS that?  Very interesting look and feeling of texture.  No clue what that is but it looks.. well gross and very alien.  Lighting is good and composition works.  I think the soft focus lets this image down though, I feel my eyes straining to find something in crisp focus and its not working.  I think it''d give this photograph a nice boost with a sharper focus and maybe even a black border to finish it off.  I gave a 4</td>', 'Yikes.. what IS that?  Very interesting look and feeling of texture.  No clue what that is but it looks.. well gross and very alien.  Lighting is good and composition works.  I think the soft focus lets this image down though, I feel my eyes straining to find something in crisp focus and its not working.  I think it''d give this photograph a nice boost with a sharper focus and maybe even a black border to finish it off.  I gave a 4', '2005-09-25 22:36:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738108, 231905, 19672, '<td valign="top">Nice shot...Would have liked to see the thumbs a bit brighter...but hey still fun<br/> <br/>Scalvert, this you?</td>', 'Nice shot...Would have liked to see the thumbs a bit brighter...but hey still fun Scalvert, this you?', '2005-09-25 22:36:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738111, 233374, 19672, '<td valign="top">Was this a 70-200mm lense ???</td>', 'Was this a 70-200mm lense ???', '2005-09-25 22:37:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738114, 234152, 11923, '<td valign="top">I love this image.  I like the simplicity of it and the use of color.  Wonderful vivid contrasts and good use of light.  Bubble is present and easily seen.  The one thing I don''t like, which I''m sure has been mentioned, is that extremely bright hot spot of white near the bubble.  If that wasn''t there I''d probably have voted it higher, but as simple and clean as the rest of the image is, that one issue is glaring and really brings the rest down.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'I love this image.  I like the simplicity of it and the use of color.  Wonderful vivid contrasts and good use of light.  Bubble is present and easily seen.  The one thing I don''t like, which I''m sure has been mentioned, is that extremely bright hot spot of white near the bubble.  If that wasn''t there I''d probably have voted it higher, but as simple and clean as the rest of the image is, that one issue is glaring and really brings the rest down.  I gave a 6.', '2005-09-25 22:38:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738119, 233402, 11923, '<td valign="top">Absolutely adorable.  Fantastic lighting, great expression.  I love the texture of the tub and the way its tones can be found in the shadows on the baby''s skin.  There are a few areas where the skin looks a bit plastic-y/wonky focus which is distracting (particularly on the right side near the diaper) but for the most part it is just perfect.  I gave an 8.</td>', 'Absolutely adorable.  Fantastic lighting, great expression.  I love the texture of the tub and the way its tones can be found in the shadows on the baby''s skin.  There are a few areas where the skin looks a bit plastic-y/wonky focus which is distracting (particularly on the right side near the diaper) but for the most part it is just perfect.  I gave an 8.', '2005-09-25 22:40:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738134, 234523, 11923, '<td valign="top">Interesting image.  Nice composition.  I love the match between the bubble and the makeup but it also draws me in and makes me strain to see more details of the model, which makes me wish the lighting wasn''t so soft on her face.  This was probably needed of course because the bubble is clearly the focus, but a little more fill light on the left might still have allowed some of the model''s details in without fighting with the bubble.  In fact it may have added more fill to the left side of the bubble bringing out the lovely metallic pastel color of it.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Interesting image.  Nice composition.  I love the match between the bubble and the makeup but it also draws me in and makes me strain to see more details of the model, which makes me wish the lighting wasn''t so soft on her face.  This was probably needed of course because the bubble is clearly the focus, but a little more fill light on the left might still have allowed some of the model''s details in without fighting with the bubble.  In fact it may have added more fill to the left side of the bubble bringing out the lovely metallic pastel color of it.  I gave a 6.', '2005-09-25 22:44:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738140, 233050, 11923, '<td valign="top">Very interested in finding out how managed to get this without it popping.  I like the idea behind the image, love the composition.  Lighting is great.  I wish the focus was a bit sharper on the bubble as it is wonderfully sharp on the shoes.  Since the bubble is such a HUGE part of this image, the softer focus is fairly distracting.  Not sure if you used a polarizer or not, but the blue of the sky looks like it could use just a smidge of depth and create a bit more contrast to the pink/peach of the shoes.  Over all though its a wonderfully creative image.  I gave a 6.</td>', 'Very interested in finding out how managed to get this without it popping.  I like the idea behind the image, love the composition.  Lighting is great.  I wish the focus was a bit sharper on the bubble as it is wonderfully sharp on the shoes.  Since the bubble is such a HUGE part of this image, the softer focus is fairly distracting.  Not sure if you used a polarizer or not, but the blue of the sky looks like it could use just a smidge of depth and create a bit more contrast to the pink/peach of the shoes.  Over all though its a wonderfully creative image.  I gave a 6.', '2005-09-25 22:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738147, 234635, 11923, '<td valign="top">The image certainly has bubbles, but it is missing something to bring the viewer in and make them interested in what they are seeing.  The lighting is good, you have some nice detailing in the bubbles on the left.  They start to brown out where the light isn''t touching them in the upper left corner, I''d say cropping that out would fix it up though.  The focus on the scrubber? or whatever the thing in the foreground is, is not so great.. I can''t quite determine what it is, and since it is such a huge element in the image, it should be in good focus.. otherwise it isn''t important and thus shouldn''t have such a prominent place in the picture.  I think there are some good technical works here its just the composition that brings it down a few notches and leaves me unsatisfied as a viewer.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'The image certainly has bubbles, but it is missing something to bring the viewer in and make them interested in what they are seeing.  The lighting is good, you have some nice detailing in the bubbles on the left.  They start to brown out where the light isn''t touching them in the upper left corner, I''d say cropping that out would fix it up though.  The focus on the scrubber? or whatever the thing in the foreground is, is not so great.. I can''t quite determine what it is, and since it is such a huge element in the image, it should be in good focus.. otherwise it isn''t important and thus shouldn''t have such a prominent place in the picture.  I think there are some good technical works here its just the composition that brings it down a few notches and leaves me unsatisfied as a viewer.  I gave a 4.', '2005-09-25 22:50:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738153, 233943, 11923, '<td valign="top">I like this.. despite its blurry nature.  I really dig the creeping color intruding or leaving the black.  Unfortunately there''s no bubbles that I can see so I can''t see how it works for the challenge.  It is possible that the streaks are ON a bubble, but due to the super soft focus I can''t really tell what it is.  I gave a 3, but had a bubble clearly been present and envisionable I probably would''ve given a 6 for the simplistic elegence (assuming the focus was good).  3.</td>', 'I like this.. despite its blurry nature.  I really dig the creeping color intruding or leaving the black.  Unfortunately there''s no bubbles that I can see so I can''t see how it works for the challenge.  It is possible that the streaks are ON a bubble, but due to the super soft focus I can''t really tell what it is.  I gave a 3, but had a bubble clearly been present and envisionable I probably would''ve given a 6 for the simplistic elegence (assuming the focus was good).  3.', '2005-09-25 22:53:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738157, 232889, 11923, '<td valign="top">Heh, cute. Bubbles galore, great focus and nice use of light.. but I think the black/white nature of this image really lets it down.  When I see a rubber ducky I''m expecting a splash of vivid yellow/orange color and so this image comes across kind of flat to me.  I don''t know if a selective desat. would''ve worked here or not, might have been too overpowering if it could''ve been done.  I do like the bits of interest such as the tub upper drain and chain but I think color *might* have been better - unless there are flaws with the tub itself.  Anyway, cute but didn''t draw me in any more than that.  I gave a 4.</td>', 'Heh, cute. Bubbles galore, great focus and nice use of light.. but I think the black/white nature of this image really lets it down.  When I see a rubber ducky I''m expecting a splash of vivid yellow/orange color and so this image comes across kind of flat to me.  I don''t know if a selective desat. would''ve worked here or not, might have been too overpowering if it could''ve been done.  I do like the bits of interest such as the tub upper drain and chain but I think color *might* have been better - unless there are flaws with the tub itself.  Anyway, cute but didn''t draw me in any more than that.  I gave a 4.', '2005-09-25 22:55:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1738163, 232704, 11923, '<td valign="top">What a doll.  Lovely focus, great use of the outdoor light (if other light sources are used, well good usage on those too).  Composition is great though if the girl''s fingers were down just a bit so you could see the bubble wand more, it might be a bit better.  I love the outfit, the hat gives the image some nice color and brightness.  I do wish it wasn''t cut off at the top though.  Very nicely done.  I gave a 6</td>', 'What a doll.  Lovely focus, great use of the outdoor light (if other light sources are used, well good usage on those too).  Composition is great though if the girl''s fingers were down just a bit so you could see the bubble wand more, it might be a bit better.  I love the outfit, the hat gives the image some nice color and brightness.  I do wish it wasn''t cut off at the top though.  Very nicely done.  I gave a 6', '2005-09-25 22:58:23.000000', NULL, 1),
