(1744106, 232810, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Awesome job explaining what you did.  I love when I photographer shares how they were able to create something.  It is really interesting that you said you placed this on a red mat, it really doesn''t like there would be one.  I would think reading the description the photo would contain many more red highlights.  I think you did an excellent job capturing the bubbles.  I think a lot of the voters who counted down on images where the bubbles were not all 100% clear did not try to take a photo of bubbles.  I think you did a great job capturing the soda with the moving bubbles. I love that you used the cherry in the image to break up the colors and draw attention in.  The glow produced by the bubbles on the left hand side is very visually pleasing.  It would be really cool, if all the bubbles looked this way.  I also like the placement of the cherry, not perfectly in the center of the image.  Great composition and good job!</td>', '*Critique Club* Awesome job explaining what you did.  I love when I photographer shares how they were able to create something.  It is really interesting that you said you placed this on a red mat, it really doesn''t like there would be one.  I would think reading the description the photo would contain many more red highlights.  I think you did an excellent job capturing the bubbles.  I think a lot of the voters who counted down on images where the bubbles were not all 100% clear did not try to take a photo of bubbles.  I think you did a great job capturing the soda with the moving bubbles. I love that you used the cherry in the image to break up the colors and draw attention in.  The glow produced by the bubbles on the left hand side is very visually pleasing.  It would be really cool, if all the bubbles looked this way.  I also like the placement of the cherry, not perfectly in the center of the image.  Great composition and good job!', '2005-09-28 02:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1744148, 234029, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Congrats on breaking through the 5.  The title is my favorite part.  I was not sure at first what the image was, but after thinking about I really do like the image.  I am wondering if many voters did not understand what the image was of. This was really a great idea.  I would be curious to see it in color.  What seems a little odd, is in the photo how the bottom bubble blower is almost shaped out of the pile of bubbles.  I think this image was a very good try at the bubble contest and probably misunderstood.  I really like how gel like the bubbles in the pile appear.  There is not much I could say to improve the photo but to try and draw the voter in a little more.  Maybe by having a bubble (a little bigger and more recognizable) coming out of one of the wands, but maybe that is not what you were going for.</td>', '*Critique Club* Congrats on breaking through the 5.  The title is my favorite part.  I was not sure at first what the image was, but after thinking about I really do like the image.  I am wondering if many voters did not understand what the image was of. This was really a great idea.  I would be curious to see it in color.  What seems a little odd, is in the photo how the bottom bubble blower is almost shaped out of the pile of bubbles.  I think this image was a very good try at the bubble contest and probably misunderstood.  I really like how gel like the bubbles in the pile appear.  There is not much I could say to improve the photo but to try and draw the voter in a little more.  Maybe by having a bubble (a little bigger and more recognizable) coming out of one of the wands, but maybe that is not what you were going for.', '2005-09-28 02:28:22.000000', NULL, 0),
