(1744634, 234192, 44860, '<td valign="top">Yes, this is what they call "voters see the photo, but don''t have your emotional background". Don''t put us this way next time, because I''m not feeling good of critiquing somebody''s great aniversary cake :(</td>', 'Yes, this is what they call "voters see the photo, but don''t have your emotional background". Don''t put us this way next time, because I''m not feeling good of critiquing somebody''s great aniversary cake :(', '2005-09-28 08:01:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1744724, 234607, 39664, '<td valign="top">I realize now that the title threw some people.  There are a series of men''s body wash (Axe I think?) that have the funniest, suggestive commercials and the slogan is "How dirty boys get clean".  My first inclination was to call this "Bubble Butt" but I thought of those commercials and how funny they are and changed my mind.....not thinking of how international this site is and how that could be misinterpreted.<br/> <br/>Thanks to my husband for being a gracious model.  Sorry, Racha, that  I "grossed" you out and to anyone else if I offended you. It was meant to be humorous but many just didn''t "get it". <br/> <br/>Thank you to those that gave constructive criticism and those that got the humor!  That is always appreciated! <br/> <br/>It''s seems rather funny/ironic that a nude female breast or body get high marks and great comments but a cute man''s rear end invoked feelings of "gross".  <br/> <br/>I see the technical problems of my photo.  I added some grain to the entire photo in attempt to tone down the flash hot spots and in attempt to bring out the bubbles more.<br/> <br/>Live and learn.</td>', 'I realize now that the title threw some people.  There are a series of men''s body wash (Axe I think?) that have the funniest, suggestive commercials and the slogan is "How dirty boys get clean".  My first inclination was to call this "Bubble Butt" but I thought of those commercials and how funny they are and changed my mind.....not thinking of how international this site is and how that could be misinterpreted. Thanks to my husband for being a gracious model.  Sorry, Racha, that  I "grossed" you out and to anyone else if I offended you. It was meant to be humorous but many just didn''t "get it".  Thank you to those that gave constructive criticism and those that got the humor!  That is always appreciated!  It''s seems rather funny/ironic that a nude female breast or body get high marks and great comments but a cute man''s rear end invoked feelings of "gross".   I see the technical problems of my photo.  I added some grain to the entire photo in attempt to tone down the flash hot spots and in attempt to bring out the bubbles more. Live and learn.', '2005-09-28 09:07:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1744794, 233402, 42840, '<td valign="top">beautiful capture. luv it through n through</td>', 'beautiful capture. luv it through n through', '2005-09-28 09:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1744797, 234523, 41066, '<td valign="top">I have to say, I am really surprised that this did not do better.  I was looking for it in the top ten!  I gave it a ten because it showed creativity and IMHO was well shot.  Congrats on a great photograph.</td>', 'I have to say, I am really surprised that this did not do better.  I was looking for it in the top ten!  I gave it a ten because it showed creativity and IMHO was well shot.  Congrats on a great photograph.', '2005-09-28 09:41:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1744838, 231849, 37265, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the interesting comments. The question of weather or not it is a bubble? Most dictionaries include in the definition something to the effect of: A speculative scheme that comes to nothing: lost money in the real estate bubble. (From answers.com)<br/> <br/>The shot was done with a piece of glass suspended approximately ¼ inch above the stock market tables. The glass was coated with Rain-X to increase the surface tension and a drop of water formed the bubble. Lighting was a single umbrella to the left.<br/></td>', 'Thank you for all the interesting comments. The question of weather or not it is a bubble? Most dictionaries include in the definition something to the effect of: A speculative scheme that comes to nothing: lost money in the real estate bubble. (From answers.com) The shot was done with a piece of glass suspended approximately ¼ inch above the stock market tables. The glass was coated with Rain-X to increase the surface tension and a drop of water formed the bubble. Lighting was a single umbrella to the left.', '2005-09-28 09:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
