(1747837, 233135, 27099, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kylh:</b></div><hr/><i> very pretty<br/>the position of the hand is nice<br/>why is the ring backwoards? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hello, the reason the ring is backwards is because it is loose on me. It was given to me by my mother-in-law, it belonged to her mother and it has an inscription inside so I didn''t want to resize it for my size and loose the inscription and unfortunately, it keeps turning on me. ;-)<br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments, <br/> <br/>Miriam</td>', 'Originally posted by kylh: very prettythe position of the hand is nicewhy is the ring backwoards?   Hello, the reason the ring is backwards is because it is loose on me. It was given to me by my mother-in-law, it belonged to her mother and it has an inscription inside so I didn''t want to resize it for my size and loose the inscription and unfortunately, it keeps turning on me. ;-) Thanks for your comments,  Miriam', '2005-09-29 10:29:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1748027, 231783, 2217, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe this image didn''t get voted higher.  It is so beautiful.  You made such a work of art.</td>', 'I can''t believe this image didn''t get voted higher.  It is so beautiful.  You made such a work of art.', '2005-09-29 11:58:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1748223, 231783, 93, '<td valign="top">Ah.. the curse of a fantastic abstract work as a DPC challenge entry.<br/> <br/>This is easily a 6.5 - 6.8 type shot (the shallow DOF really hurts this I think, keeping it from 7 in my mind),  but people here *hate* abstracts.. it''s always been the way.  If you can, look up Dax and check out her work..  stunning color abstracts that just don''t ever get the voting that they deserve.. and you can see it with your shot.<br/> <br/>This site is a one-trick pony site, really.  Voters are looking for, and want, only one thing.  The true challenge, if you want to ribbon, is giving them that thing... which is usually something a lot of people really couldn''t care to photograph.</td>', 'Ah.. the curse of a fantastic abstract work as a DPC challenge entry. This is easily a 6.5 - 6.8 type shot (the shallow DOF really hurts this I think, keeping it from 7 in my mind),  but people here *hate* abstracts.. it''s always been the way.  If you can, look up Dax and check out her work..  stunning color abstracts that just don''t ever get the voting that they deserve.. and you can see it with your shot. This site is a one-trick pony site, really.  Voters are looking for, and want, only one thing.  The true challenge, if you want to ribbon, is giving them that thing... which is usually something a lot of people really couldn''t care to photograph.', '2005-09-29 13:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1748226, 231783, 43546, '<td valign="top">Hi Jean,<br/> <br/>Its so nice to get a reply from you after the votings, i am glad you can share the same artistic imagination from the picture i had created.<br/> <br/>Alot of encouragements from your compliments! Thanks.<br/> <br/>Cheers!</td>', 'Hi Jean, Its so nice to get a reply from you after the votings, i am glad you can share the same artistic imagination from the picture i had created. Alot of encouragements from your compliments! Thanks. Cheers!', '2005-09-29 13:50:18.000000', NULL, 0),
